{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge","id":881151,"title":"Are There Spirits in the Hedge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T12:05:36-07:00","id":881151,"title":"Are There Spirits in the Hedge?","content":"Essentially, I'm curious to know if the Hedge has spirits, or even a Shadow - that latter seems unlikely to me, but I haven't found anything on the topic and am curious if I've missed anything.<br /> Similarly, what about the state of Twilight?<br /> <br /> If it doesn't have a Shadow, what happens to spirits who wander through a Hedge gate, say by following a human, or being a mage's familiar etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:12:28-07:00","id":881156,"title":"","content":"i have been curious about this as well. What would a spirit or werewolf do if they were trapped in the hedge? how would they find essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:17:15-07:00","id":881161,"title":"","content":"The shadow is a reflection of the material world and spirits feed on the resonance made by the material world. The hedge (and almost all realms but the material) also does not have a state of twilight so the spirit would be in a materialized form anywhere in the hedge.<br /> <br /> Now if a spirit were to find its way into the hedge it would have to worry about almost everything that anything else that finds its way into the hedge has to worry about and more. The thorns could tear into it as if it were their bane. There are beasts twisted by the hedge that may prey upon these stranded beings. They could be captured and sold in a goblin market. Other than that they would likely struggle to find resonant essence to feed on if they can find any at all.<br /> <br /> What would happen to a spirit if it ventured into the hedge? The same thing that happens to everything else - nothing good.<br /> <br /> *Note: A mage's familiar would likely be more protected than other ephemeral beings in the hedge and also be one of the few that wouldn't starve by virtue of being a mage's familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:19:42-07:00","id":881164,"title":"","content":"Werewolves would probably have to resort to eating briarwolves in the Hedge, or lost humans and changelings. They don't lose Essence without really using it, so it's not as if they, like vampires, need to expend a certain amount every day. Unless they're on a sacred hunt, a werewolf stuck in a strange world like the Hedge would probably focus on trying to escape through a portal.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's a Hisil, or Gauntlet, based on first edition rules. I'm sure a writer will come around an answer that specific question for second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:46:17-07:00","id":881179,"title":"","content":"The Hedge does not have a Shadow. Any spirit that enters it is going to materialize, and if it dawdles too long, Glamour will replace their Essence and turn them into hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> The only source of Essence for a Werewolf is the flesh of lost humans and the Lost.<br /> <br /> Equinox Road, Chapter 2, if you want more, as well as Rites of Spring, Chapter 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:47:22-07:00","id":881180,"title":"","content":"According to one of the books (I can't recall which), Uratha see Glamour and Essence as something similar, so it's conceivable that some spirits could survive in the Hedge. And as noted, Werewolves could eat briarwolves or lost humans, so I could see spirits attaching themselves to changelings and hobgoblins that fit their influences. I don't think any Goblin salesman would object to having a big, burly spirit bodyguard if they can figure out how to feed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:47:47-07:00","id":881181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=881179#post881179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge does not have a Shadow. Any spirit that enters it is going to materialize, and if it dawdles too long, Glamour will replace their Essence and turn them into hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> The only source of Essence for a Werewolf is the flesh of lost humans and the Lost.<br /> <br /> Equinox Road, Chapter 2, if you want more, as well as Rites of Spring, Chapter 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T03:16:47-07:00","id":881622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=881180#post881180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to one of the books (I can't recall which), Uratha see Glamour and Essence as something similar, so it's conceivable that some spirits could survive in the Hedge. And as noted, Werewolves could eat briarwolves or lost humans, so I could see spirits attaching themselves to changelings and hobgoblins that fit their influences. I don't think any Goblin salesman would object to having a big, burly spirit bodyguard if they can figure out how to feed it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah the spirit survives by becoming a hobgoblin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T06:17:23-07:00","id":881715,"title":"","content":"If spirits in the Hedge become hobgoblins, would hobgoblins in Shadow become spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T06:24:49-07:00","id":881720,"title":"","content":"They'd probably become spirit chow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:53:09-07:00","id":881784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=881720#post881720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd probably become spirit chow.</div> </div> </div> </div>As would most spirits in the Hedge become Goblin-chow.<br /> <br /> Is there some kind of exchange program set up? Ghosts getting lost in the Shadow, Goetics wandering into the Hedge, Hobgoblins vacationing in the Underworld, etc.?<br /> <br /> If not, that could form the core for a fun (if silly) campaign idea...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:00:11-07:00","id":881791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=881784#post881784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As would most spirits in the Hedge become Goblin-chow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, unless hobgoblins have changed a lot.<br /> <br /> It's not about some perceived 'better than' competition, just that spirits are predatory by nature and gain Essence for being such, while hobgoblins weren't. More would likely turn into hobgoblins or get lost in the Thorns, if such a thing is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:34:08-07:00","id":881904,"title":"","content":"Disregarding the pissing match because that has too many variable, hobgoblins wouldn't become spirits in the Shadow. The Hedge is something of an Arcadia-Lite in that it's a place saturated by the Wyrd, which connects things in the way that is both text and subtext, meaning that as whatever's in there too long starts to change perspective, they start to transform into fae-types. The Hedge is inherently transformative, is my point. The Shadow lacks the hardline of transformation that the Hedge posesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:15:50-07:00","id":882487,"title":"","content":"I think the type of the spirit has an influence over what sort of hobgoblin it becomes. Spirits of greed might become minor hobgoblin merchants and work their way up the social ladder of the goblin markets, such as it is. Wolf spirits might become briar-wolves, and other animal spirits might turn into briar-somethings.<br /> <br /> Does the Hedge turns objects like Imbued Items, Fetishes and Gadgets into Tokens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:28:34-07:00","id":882493,"title":"","content":"There were automatons, if I recall correctly, animated objects and limited 'golems.' Or maybe magic objects find their way to goblin markets, one way or another.<br /> <br /> I always thought briarwolves were what was supposed to happen to werewolves who got lost in the Thorns. There was a mage one, too, whose name I forget. Wonder if there's still the variety of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Hobgoblin_(CTL)\" target=\"_blank\">hobgoblins</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:36:40-07:00","id":882496,"title":"","content":"Briarwolves might be the result of werewolf, The Unmade were something of a mistake to make in regards to Mage/Changeling questions, and yeah, there's a wide variety of hobgoblins for days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:28:33-07:00","id":883204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=881904#post881904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disregarding the pissing match because that has too many variable, hobgoblins wouldn't become spirits in the Shadow. The Hedge is something of an Arcadia-Lite in that it's a place saturated by the Wyrd, which connects things in the way that is both text and subtext, meaning that as whatever's in there too long starts to change perspective, they start to transform into fae-types. The Hedge is inherently transformative, is my point. The Shadow lacks the hardline of transformation that the Hedge posesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge having blatant cosmological superiority over other realms isn't part of pissing match? And by superiority I mean the simple fact that hobgoblins are not affected in any way by Underworld or Shadow, unlike ghosts and spirits which become transformed if they are in the Hedge longer than moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:38:22-07:00","id":883213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883204#post883204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hedge having blatant cosmological superiority over other realms isn't part of pissing match? And by superiority I mean the simple fact that hobgoblins are not affected in any way by Underworld or Shadow, unlike ghosts and spirits which become transformed if they are in the Hedge longer than moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than a moment, I think.<br /> <br /> It probably has more to do with the Essence dependency and malleable nature of ephemerals in general (and Spirits in particular). Spirits are already known to change based upon what they feed upon - one trapped in the Underworld is going to be more ghost-like before long, while one with nothing but Glamour to eat is going to take on some of those qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:01:35-07:00","id":883237,"title":"","content":"^ This. Hobgoblins don't really have the same dependency on Glamour that a Ghost or Spirit does on Essence, probably because they're a physical creature as opposed to an Ephemeral Being. They aren't sustained by it, in the conventional sense, unless like Changelings at Wyrd 6+ they become dependent on it for survival. Below that, a Hobgoblin could probably survive, listless, grumpy, and likely without being able to use Contracts, on the same sort of stuff other physical lifeforms can.<br /> <br /> Also, the Grave Dream Dead Dominion from Book of the Dead kind of pokes a hole in 'hobgoblins are not affected in any way by the Underworld'. Never heard of a hobgoblin in the Shadow, and it's never come up in one of my games, so I can't comment there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:13:04-07:00","id":883392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883204#post883204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hedge having blatant cosmological superiority over other realms isn't part of pissing match? And by superiority I mean the simple fact that hobgoblins are not affected in any way by Underworld or Shadow, unlike ghosts and spirits which become transformed if they are in the Hedge longer than moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This is not a matter of moments. Days? Maybe. Weeks? Likely. Months? Surely. Moments? No. It isn't Arcadia, so it takes time, and that time can be drawn out by not eating goblin fruit(though admittedly, getting a spirit to not eat is....funny.)<br /> <br /> 2) Hobgoblins <i>do</i> get fucked over by the Underworld, it's just not easily perceivable due to their inherent strangeness to us. But a hobgoblin stuck in the Underworld is gonna get fucked up- it affects as much as it does humans and Sin-Eaters. The Underworld in general is going to fuck anyone up. You want to complain to me about a cosmological supremacy on the virtue of what shit each place does, come back when we're talking about the Underworld.<br /> <br /> And while the Shadow does not start imposing itself in the same way as the Hedge or the Underworld, I chuckle grimly at suggesting the place that is perpetually 'the bad part of town' down to it's base core is somehow inferior. Not to say that hobgoblins will be inherently owned upon entering-even the hobs can speak to the spirits tendencies of equivalent exchange-but I wouldn't discount the supremacy of a place that's made out of teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:54:58-07:00","id":883418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883392#post883392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) This is not a matter of moments. Days? Maybe. Weeks? Likely. Months? Surely. Moments? No. It isn't Arcadia, so it takes time, and that time can be drawn out by not eating goblin fruit(though admittedly, getting a spirit to not eat is....funny.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does a starvation spirit need to eat, strictly speaking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:05:23-07:00","id":883421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883418#post883418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a starvation spirit need to eat, strictly speaking?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a spirit. They only have one universal rule. Everything eats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T02:12:27-07:00","id":883603,"title":"","content":"Spirits eat what resonates with their concept. Either resonance of their type or spirits they thematically should eat (without becoming corrupted / diluted).<br /> <br /> A starvation spirit can feed on either resonance of starvation or say spirits of health symbolizing people who starve not being healthy. Like a wolf spirit eating a rabbit spirit a spirit can eat something as long as it doesn't contradict it's nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-06-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:03:02-07:00","id":884052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883418#post883418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Does a starvation spirit need to eat, strictly speaking?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> A starvation spirit could also be a gluttony spirit that makes you consume so much of a certain resource (gluttony is not just about food) that others can't have it. It could also be a disgust spirit that specializes in instilling delusions of obesity so the victim inflicts starvation on themselves. It could be a spirit of drugs too, which makes you spend so much money on getting your next fix that you can't buy food.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883603#post883603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits eat what resonates with their concept. Either resonance of their type or spirits they thematically should eat (without becoming corrupted / diluted).<br /> <br /> A starvation spirit can feed on either resonance of starvation or say spirits of health symbolizing people who starve not being healthy. Like a wolf spirit eating a rabbit spirit a spirit can eat something as long as it doesn't contradict it's nature.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are correct, but a snake spirit is unlikely to find any normal rabbit or rat spirits to eat. The Hedge doesn't just transform here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:16:18-07:00","id":884068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=884052#post884052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> A starvation spirit could also be a gluttony spirit that makes you consume so much of a certain resource (gluttony is not just about food) that others can't have it. It could also be a disgust spirit that specializes in instilling delusions of obesity so the victim inflicts starvation on themselves. It could be a spirit of drugs too, which makes you spend so much money on getting your next fix that you can't buy food.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> You are correct, but a snake spirit is unlikely to find any normal rabbit or rat spirits to eat. The Hedge doesn't just transform here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I think it's the &quot;consuming prey animal&quot; that counts regarding deviation. Who cares if this rabbit has a pocketwatch and punctuality obsession?<br /> <br /> The Resonance of the hunt/kill might generate 1 point of Essence (though obviously the Essence-less prey wouldn't yield any more).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:35:42-07:00","id":884080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=884068#post884068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but I think it's the &quot;consuming prey animal&quot; that counts regarding deviation. Who cares if this rabbit has a pocketwatch and punctuality obsession?<br /> <br /> The Resonance of the hunt/kill might generate 1 point of Essence (though obviously the Essence-less prey wouldn't yield any more).</div> </div> </div> </div> You are right. The key word here is <i>eventually</i>. The spirit can survive on these occasional meals, but it will be getting a lot less Essence than it is used to. <i>Eventually</i>, it will encounter a hobgoblin or another threat that forces it to spend the little Essence that is left to protect itself. With no appropriate prey nearby, the spirit will have to consume things that accumulate improper Resonance inside it until it becomes a hobgoblin. The Hedge is not going anywhere and it is not in any hurry. A clever changeling might offer to get the spirit out of the Hedge as part of a Pledge in exchange for a favor suited to the spirit's purview. The changeling could also ask for something simple like retrieving a lost Token if they don't trust the spirit, which is likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:43:53-07:00","id":884233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881151-are-there-spirits-in-the-hedge?p=883204#post883204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hedge having blatant cosmological superiority over other realms isn't part of pissing match? And by superiority I mean the simple fact that hobgoblins are not affected in any way by Underworld or Shadow, unlike ghosts and spirits which become transformed if they are in the Hedge longer than moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, that's hysterical. <br /> <br /> The Hedge mutated ephemeral beings while the hisil and the underworld don't mutate hobgoblins is in now way shape or form cosmological superiority, that's features of the realms themselves.<br /> <br /> A human stuck in the hisil doesn't become a spirit, nor does an animal, or plant, or machine, nor a vampire or a mage or a changeling or a promethean or a sineater or deviant or a hunter or a demon, etc, etc, the hisil is only transformative to other types of ephemeral beings, since they acclimate to their new surroundings.<br /> <br /> The hedge is transformative as hell- animals and plants become hobgoblins, people can become fae touched, and even inanimate objects in the hedge can become tokens. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}